# Cloudflare Workers Assets honors this file. ALL matching rules apply, so the
# sitewide security block below coexists with the per-path cache rules.
#
# ── Security headers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app renders CRDT-authored HTML (note bodies, grid text cells) on the same
# origin where the Supabase session lives in localStorage, so a single sanitizer
# miss is a session compromise. sanitizeNoteHtml.js is the primary defence;
# these are the backstop, and until now there were none of them at all.
#
# The enforced CSP is deliberately the subset that CANNOT break this app:
#   frame-ancestors 'none'  — clickjacking. Nothing here is meant to be framed;
#                             the app frames OTHER sites (link cards), which
#                             this does not affect.
#   base-uri 'self'         — stops an injected <base> repointing every
#                             relative URL, including the module script.
#   object-src 'none'       — no <object>/<embed> plugin surface.
#   form-action             — where a form may submit. Stripe is listed because
#                             checkout is an external destination.
# script-src/style-src are NOT enforced here: index.html carries four inline
# <script> blocks (JSON-LD, the pre-React theme bootstrap, Meta Pixel) and the
# Worker injects more, so enforcing would require 'unsafe-inline' — which buys
# nothing — or a nonce the static assets service cannot mint. The full policy
# ships as Report-Only below so violations can be read from the console before
# anything is enforced.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self' https://checkout.stripe.com
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://js.stripe.com https://checkout.stripe.com https://connect.facebook.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://use.typekit.net; font-src 'self' data: https://use.typekit.net; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://*.partykit.dev wss://*.partykit.dev https://*.r2.cloudflarestorage.com https://api.stripe.com https://www.facebook.com; frame-src https:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

# Hashed build assets (/assets/index-<hash>.js etc.) never change content for a
# given URL, so cache them hard for a year. index.html is intentionally NOT
# matched here so new deploys are always picked up immediately.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# Self-hosted fonts (Courier Prime for screenplay mode) — content-stable.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# Machine-readable documentation: the raw markdown mirror of every /docs page
# (/docs/api/cards.md), plus the llms.txt corpus files. Short cache — an agent
# reading these should get today's docs, and they change on deploy rather than
# per-request. CORS is open so a browser-side agent can fetch them.
#
# DELIBERATELY NO Content-Type OVERRIDE HERE. The assets service already infers
# text/markdown from the .md extension, and `/docs/*` splats across slashes —
# so a Content-Type rule that over-matched would serve every HTML docs page as
# markdown and break the entire site. Cache-Control over-matching is harmless
# by comparison: the Worker sets its own on HTML via withRevalidate().
/docs/*.md
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
/llms-full.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
